Eip3009Sigil::check1271
├── given the config was never initialized
│   └── it should revert with PolicyNotInitialized
├── given a fully well-formed voucher to an allowlisted payee within the cap and window
│   └── it should return VALIDATION_SUCCESS
├── given the requesting sender is not the configured token
│   └── it should return VALIDATION_FAILED
├── given the app domain separator does not match the configured token domain
│   └── it should return VALIDATION_FAILED
├── given the inner blob length is not exactly the six-word content length
│   └── it should return VALIDATION_FAILED
├── given the supplied fields do not hash to the signed contentsHash (soundness anchor)
│   └── it should return VALIDATION_FAILED
├── given the authorization payer (from) is not the signing account
│   └── it should return VALIDATION_FAILED
├── given the voucher is expired (block.timestamp >= validBefore)
│   └── it should return VALIDATION_FAILED
├── given the voucher is not yet valid (block.timestamp <= validAfter)
│   └── it should return VALIDATION_FAILED
├── given the voucher is strictly inside the (validAfter, validBefore) window
│   └── it should return VALIDATION_SUCCESS
├── given the payee equals solady's reserved set sentinel
│   └── it should return VALIDATION_FAILED without bubbling a revert
├── given the payee is not on the allowlist
│   └── it should return VALIDATION_FAILED
├── given an empty payee allowlist
│   └── it should deny every payee (default-deny)
└── given the value exceeds the per-authorization cap
    ├── when the value is exactly the cap
    │   └── it should return VALIDATION_SUCCESS
    └── when the value is one above the cap
        └── it should return VALIDATION_FAILED
